Today I did the Nth Fibonacci Number Calculator Lab.
In this Lab I should  should use a dynamic programming approach
to compute and return the n-th number from the Fibonacci sequence, 
where each number is the sum of the two preceding numbers and then
appended thecomputed Fibonacci number to the sequence list.
First I checked if the input is a valid number. Then I checked if the input is 
less or equal to 1, if true the functions directly returns n.
In the other cases I implementet a for-loop to append the sum of the last two elements in the list to the sequence list.
At the end of the loop, the functions returns the list.
After that I reviewed dynamic programming and passed the test.
